8. Automatic Complaint Analysis Module

This is the primary functionality of the application.

Users should be able to select a previously uploaded dataset and initiate automatic complaint analysis.

Analysis Workflow

1. User selects a dataset.
2. Application verifies the dataset configuration.
3. Application retrieves the complaint text column.
4. The backend loads the existing trained ML model.
5. Complaints are processed in manageable batches.
6. The ML model predicts complaint categories.
7. The system calculates prediction confidence.
8. Low-confidence complaints are flagged for review.
9. Potential new complaint groups are identified.
10. Results are saved in PostgreSQL.
11. Analysis status is updated.
12. The frontend displays the completed analysis.

Important Requirements

- Reuse the existing trained model.
- Do not train a new model automatically during normal prediction.
- Do not use paid AI APIs.
- Do not send confidential customer complaints to external services.
- Use batch processing to control memory consumption.
- Handle large datasets efficiently.
- Preserve the original uploaded dataset.
- Prevent accidental duplicate execution of the same active analysis.
- Maintain analysis ownership.

Analysis Status

Support:

- Pending
- Processing
- Completed
- Failed

Display progress information while analysis is running.

Provide useful error messages when analysis fails.

Where possible, retain valid partial results and clearly identify failed analyses.

