19. Performance and Reliability Requirements

The application must be designed for practical organizational usage.

Large Dataset Handling

- Avoid loading entire large datasets into frontend memory.
- Use backend batch processing.
- Use pagination for result tables.
- Use chunk-based CSV processing.
- Use efficient database inserts.
- Avoid unnecessary repeated model loading.
- Cache the loaded model appropriately.
- Avoid excessive database queries.

Analysis Execution

The analysis process should not block ordinary API requests.

For the initial deployment-ready implementation, use the existing background-processing architecture if appropriate.

Clearly document its limitations.

If durable background job processing is introduced, use an appropriate queue system only when justified.

Error Handling

Handle:

- Invalid files
- Missing columns
- Empty datasets
- Empty complaint text
- Model loading failures
- Prediction failures
- Database connection errors
- Report generation failures
- Interrupted analyses

Errors should be logged safely without exposing confidential complaint information.

